<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">26 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 26 February, from 364 to 1993.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/valentinian-i" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/valentinian-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">364 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,662 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Valentinian I proclaimed Roman Emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Army officers chose Valentinian, a Pannonian general, as emperor at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicaea">Nicaea</a>. A month later he made his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valens">Valens</a> co-emperor in the East, while he ruled the West.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valens">Valens</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1616 CE <span class="tih-ago">410 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Galileo is warned to abandon Copernican theory</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Cardinal Bellarmine instructed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galileo-galilei">Galileo</a>, on the Pope's orders, not to hold or defend the view that the Earth moves around the Sun. His 1632 'Dialogue' led to his trial for breaching the order.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1815 CE <span class="tih-ago">211 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon escapes from Elba</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">With about a thousand men, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> slipped away from his island exile and sailed for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. He regained power without a shot, beginning the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-days-reform">Hundred Days</a> that ended at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-waterloo">Waterloo</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1919 CE <span class="tih-ago">107 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Grand Canyon becomes a US national park</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/woodrow-wilson">Woodrow Wilson</a> signed the act creating Grand Canyon National Park in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arizona">Arizona</a>. The gorge, carved by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colorado">Colorado</a> River, is over 1.6 km deep in places.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/woodrow-wilson">Woodrow Wilson</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1935 CE <span class="tih-ago">91 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Robert Watson-Watt's team demonstrates radar</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Daventry, radio waves from a BBC transmitter bounced off an RAF bomber and were detected on a screen. The test led to the Chain Home network, vital in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-britain">Battle of Britain</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1993 CE <span class="tih-ago">33 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Truck bomb explodes beneath the World Trade Center</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Islamist militants detonated a bomb in the North Tower's underground car park, killing six people and injuring more than 1,000. The towers survived but were destroyed in the attacks of 2001.</p></div></li></ol>
